MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "WAKING THE FALLEN and Shadows Are Security pair aggressive vocals and heavy riffs with melodic guitar passages, which connects with my listening to In Flames and Soilwork.",
    "Karmacode offers heavy grooves with melodic vocals, matching the balance of weight and hooks I enjoy across my metal and hard rock listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "St. Anger's raw, repetitive heaviness misses the melody and musical variety I want, even though its intensity seems related to albums in my history.",
    "Fallen and Finger Eleven fit part of my taste, but feel lighter than what I want today; Death Magnetic and United Abominations appeal through riffing but are less compelling for this visit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Heavy guitars alone seem to count too much as a match; I care about how the aggression works with melody and changing passages.",
    "My past interest in melodic alternative rock seems to carry too much weight for a visit when I am choosing heavier music."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated listening to In Flames and Soilwork makes the combination of aggressive vocals and melodic leads especially relevant to my choices today.",
    "An album can suit my taste without being something I would choose now: I would start with WAKING THE FALLEN rather than also choose another Avenged Sevenfold album in the same visit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in heavy, melodic music, but sometimes treat heaviness or broad rock appeal as enough without capturing the balance I want today."
}
